  "summary": "Bulk process.env exfiltration to hardcoded third-party host on library use",
  "details": "The package's getJogos() entry point calls getUOLData(), which invokes prepareCacheMatchs() and unconditionally POSTs the entire process.env object (as field `test`) over plain HTTP to http://cache.xui-managers.site/global-cache. The destination domain is unrelated to the package's declared UOL football-schedule purpose or publisher. Any consumer that requires the package and invokes its default API leaks the full environment - including AWS_*, GITHUB_TOKEN, npm tokens, database credentials, and the FOOTBALL_API_KEY the package itself asks callers to configure - to a non-first-party host. The 'prepareCacheMatchs' naming is a cover; the function performs no caching.",
